5.text:
{Moss Block.}

I’m now strongly favoring **Moss Block** as the intended answer. Obsidian is not actually obtainable first with an empty inventory, since it needs a diamond pickaxe or better. Snow layers may be hand-breakable if the platform is in a snowy biome, but snow only gives snowballs and does not unlock real progression—no wood, no crafting table, no tools, no way to advance. Podzol is close, but it still requires an additional key trade: a sapling. Moss block is stronger because it can bootstrap wood without needing a sapling trade.

The intended route is: obtain emeralds from the constrained mob/trader setup, wait for a wandering trader selling a **moss block**, place it, then get bones from skeletons at night, craft bone meal in the 2×2 grid, and use bone meal on the moss block. In modern versions, bone meal on moss can generate an azalea, and bone meal on the azalea grows an azalea tree, yielding logs. Once you have wood, you can craft a crafting table and tools and begin normal progression.

The specific disabling of Enderman and Spider spawns also supports this: it removes alternative mob-drop routes such as ender pearls or string, while leaving skeletons available, which are exactly what the moss-block route needs for bone meal. So I would vote **Moss Block**.}

2.text:
{The first block must be **Snow Layer**.

On a 3×3 obsidian platform in a snowy biome, snow layers naturally form on the platform. With an empty inventory, these can be broken by hand to obtain snowballs. Four snowballs can be crafted into a snow block in the 2×2 inventory grid, and that snow block can be placed to extend the platform. By repeating this, you can build a bridge away from the original 3×3 platform.

This is the critical bootstrap: once you are more than 24 blocks away from the original platform, hostile mobs can finally spawn there. That allows pillagers to spawn for emeralds and skeletons for bones. With emeralds, you can trade with a wandering trader for podzol/moss and a sapling, then grow a tree and obtain wood. Without first getting the snow layer, you cannot expand or move away, so no hostile mobs can spawn, and you cannot obtain emeralds or any other useful block. Thus the snow layer is the necessary first block to advance.}

